  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">B&amp;Z - Emergency response to the conflict 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of March 3, 2026, according to the Disaster Risk Management Unit (DRM), there are 58,064 internally displaced persons (12,539 families) registered within collective shelters, while others who have resorted to extended family members or have not yet found a place to stay remain unregistered. A total of 321 shelters are currently open, of which 52 shelters still have hosting capacity. In addition, 259 hostilities have been recorded, resulting in 246 injuries and 40 fatalities.

In response to the evolving situation, B&amp;Z is closely coordinating with DRM/DRR committees, the Ministry of Social Affairs (MoSA), and various sectoral working groups (Food Security, WASH, Protection, Cash, Education, others) to ensure a well-aligned and effective humanitarian response.</narrative>
  </description>
